{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102238-the-house-rule-thread","id":1102238,"title":"The House Rule Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-10T05:11:15-07:00","id":1102238,"title":"The House Rule Thread","content":"I wanted to start a thread where we can discuss house rules, since I feel like Mage tends to lend itself to these more than most other gamelines. A couple of things I wanted to get out there before we start, though:<br /> <br /> This is mostly for actual house rules, not rules interpretations - allowing Death to heal probably isn't a house rule so much as an interpretation. A house rule in this context would be, for example, placing Gnosis caps. Additionally, this isn't the place to argue about someone else's house rule.<br /> <br /> I'll start:<br /> <br /> At our table, we don't allow any bonuses that aren't Yantras or Ritual bonuses to factor into the spell when determining maximum spell factors. You can stack spell factors all you want until your total dice pool after accounting for Gnosis + Arcana + Ritual Bonus + Yantras - Spell Factors is -5, but no further.<br /> <br /> After that's done, any additional bonuses (From Fate spells, Conditions, Merits, etc) is applied.<br /> <br /> This tends to curb any kind of ridiculous bonus stacking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T08:56:37-07:00","id":1102278,"title":"","content":"I have a house rule regarding Shifting Sands and kind of a house-rule for Hallows:<br /> Shifting Sands requires 1 point of Mana with each use and travelling back a full scene requires 1 additional point of mana. The flow of mana at a Hallow is also constant regardless of Time Manipulation, thus you cannot gain mana from a Hallow more than once using Shifting Sands.<br /> <br /> This keeps people with the initial Time 3 from just saying, &quot;Alright guys with my 1 Dot Hallow I will get full mana.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T09:53:26-07:00","id":1102287,"title":"","content":"One minor hack is to cap magical healing - you can &quot;patch over&quot; damage, but you can only magically heal up to your Health total (these caps fall off at the same rate natural healing happens).<br /> <br /> Proximus hacks:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li>Proximi can become closer to full Mages through incremental improvement (see the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits\">Homebrew Mage Merits</a> thread for details).<ul><li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=948623#post948623\">Dynastic Heir</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=948623#post948623\">Arcane Prodigy</a> can increase effect Gnosis and Arcana, respectively.</li> <li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=965813#post965813\">Wise Sleepwalker</a> lets Proximi try to contain their Paradoxes.</li> <li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1083833#post1083833\">Spell Control</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1083833#post1083833\">Mystic Tools</a> let you sustain more spells, and use Yantras, respectively.</li> <li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1083833#post1083833\">Attaining Insight</a> unlocks the Arcana based Attainments for Proximi (at least, for their Blessing Arcana).</li> </ul></li> <li>Allow Proximi to pick up out-of-Dynasty Blessings at a surcharge (+1 XP for in-Arcana, +2 XP for out-of-Arcana). Always costs Mana, and granting any Free Reach is optional.</li> <li>Proximi can incur Paradox normally (the Cancel-Blessing-and-Aggravate-Curse is an ST option).</li> <li>Proximi don't risk Paradox (closer to Legacy Attainments), but exceeding 1 Reach causes <u>Strain</u> - Reduce Willpower by 1 per, recovering at 1 per day.</li> <li>Link Effective Gnosis to Integrity on the same scale as Nephilim and Primum - Glitches correspond to Nimbus Conditions, culminating in Mad-like status (like Second-hand Secrecy).</li> <li>Give each Proximus Dynasty some Boon - either a passive bonus to enforce its concept, some trick like bonus Potency/Duration or extra Reach for using their Blessings in theme, or another flavor-enhancing perk.</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Another one for cross-over is intended to limit Mage interaction with others and make Sleepwalkers more valuable and special: No Free Sleepwalking - Unless the being is 1) A Mage, Proximus, or possesses Wisdom 2) an Ephemeral Entity 3) Never human or 4) Actually has the Sleepwalker or Fitful Slumber Merit, they count as a Sleeper. Vampire? Sleeper. Changeling? Sleeper. Mummy? Sleeper. Sin-Eater? Sleeper (the Geist isn't, but the human is, which can lead to <i>interesting</i> conversations). Demons, Werewolves, and Prometheans are tricky. This serves to isolate Mages more, and make someone who doesn't cause Dissonance significant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-20-2017, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T09:13:17-07:00","id":1102832,"title":"","content":"I don't allow Gnosis to be bought with regular XP and half of Arcana XP must come from arcane XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T10:13:25-07:00","id":1102852,"title":"","content":"I have relaxing mundane activities restore a point of willpower (cooking and sharing a meal, going to the movies with friends, etc.) in addition to a night's rest. It's a minor thing for my players to not completely give up on their humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T07:06:27-07:00","id":1103116,"title":"","content":"I like that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T15:08:45-07:00","id":1103299,"title":"","content":"I always had this simple houserule: 1 bashing damage heals after an hour or when a full scene has passed, not just 15 minutes. I like that wounds may carry over from scene to scene, like a bruised elbow from a scrape with a hunter a few scenes ago still aches and throbs when trying to climb a fence later, for example. This also applies for Uratha regenerating lethal wounds without Essence expenditure, BTW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T04:39:02-07:00","id":1103440,"title":"","content":"Except for in Werewolf for obvious reasons, we're running with losing a dot of Integrity, Humanity, Wisdom, et cetera, awards the 2 XP it costs to rebuy. It's especially effective with Humanity were you can act monstrous if it fits the character and situation without feeling that it's a waste of XP since (at least in my group) you'd want to rebuy Humanity later anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T05:55:23-07:00","id":1103452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102238-the-house-rule-thread?p=1103440#post1103440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except for in Werewolf for obvious reasons, we're running with losing a dot of Integrity, Humanity, Wisdom, et cetera, awards the 2 XP it costs to rebuy. It's especially effective with Humanity were you can act monstrous if it fits the character and situation without feeling that it's a waste of XP since (at least in my group) you'd want to rebuy Humanity later anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I could also see you getting the XP in flavored form instead (Arcane, Vitriol, etc.), too. That way you still get compensated, but can't just buy it back immediately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T06:01:40-07:00","id":1103454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102238-the-house-rule-thread?p=1103452#post1103452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, I could also see you getting the XP in flavored form instead (Arcane, Vitriol, etc.), too. That way you still get compensated, but can't just buy it back immediately.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be a good idea for some systems, but we only play two systems with special XP and I don't think Blood XP (gained through Diablerie) fits since Diablerie is often the cause of Humanity loss, and Arcane XP doesn't do much of a difference since it's used just as much as regular XP in our group. Instead of buying an Arcana dot with 2 regular and 2 Arcane you'd just buy it for 4 Arcane and spend the regular on Wisdom, when you feel like increasing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T03:00:24-07:00","id":1105641,"title":"","content":"The only real house rule I have in my game is for identifying spells as they're cast. The others are just updates of 1e rules (especially Astral mechanics).<br /> <br /> I made this rule quite a while ago, back when I was first learning mage. Now that I think about how improvised spells and rotes work, these rules may not actually make sense. Identifying spells usually requires decoding it as a Mystery.<br /> <br /> <b>Identifying Spells</b><br /> You must have active mage sight of the correct Arcanum (or Prime sight). Roll Gnosis + Arcanum to identify the spell as a reflexive action for Instant spells, or an extended action for ritual spells (time of each roll = your ritual interval).<ul><li>The number of successes required for identifying an instant spell is equal to the dots of the highest Arcanum of the spell.</li> <li>The number of successes required to identify a ritual spell is equal to the dots of the highest Arcanum used in the spell multiplied by the number of ritual intervals used by the caster(s).</li> </ul>Dice pool modifiers:<ul><li>Add +1 for Prime sight.</li> <li>Add +1 for Mastery of the highest arcanum involved.</li> <li>Add +1 for Archmastery of the highest arcanum involved (stacks with Mastery bonus).</li> <li>Add +1 if your Gnosis is above 5.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T09:13:00-07:00","id":1105724,"title":"","content":"I think it would be cool to see those Astral mechanic updates, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T09:24:08-07:00","id":1105726,"title":"","content":"A minor hack might be replacing Mana costs (for spells) with Paradox dice. You can still spend a Mana to reduce the die afterwards, but it does expand the chances of Paradox (due to the Chance Die).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T09:54:55-07:00","id":1105741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102238-the-house-rule-thread?p=1105726#post1105726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A minor hack might be replacing Mana costs (for spells) with Paradox dice. You can still spend a Mana to reduce the die afterwards, but it does expand the chances of Paradox (due to the Chance Die).</div> </div> </div> </div>Scelesti are going to love direct damage spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T10:33:54-07:00","id":1105756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102238-the-house-rule-thread?p=1105741#post1105741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Scelesti are going to love direct damage spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? Damage doesn't scale with Mana usage, and they still have to control their Paradoxes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there b